WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Poisoning can happen in many ways, whether something is swallowed,

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.360
breathed in, or even just touches the skin or eyes.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.880
You might notice a wide range of symptoms, such as dizziness,

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.040
a headache, difficulty breathing, or even nausea and vomiting.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:19.440
Your first priority is always scene safety. If you see spilled or leaking

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.639
containers, do not approach the area and make sure

00:00:22.639 --> 00:00:27.120
to tell others to stay away as well. When providing care, the person's level

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.240
of consciousness determines your next move. If they are

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.279
alert and stable, your first call should be to poison

00:00:33.279 --> 00:00:37.520
control at 1-800-222-1222.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.639
However, if they are not alert or appear unstable,

00:00:40.639 --> 00:00:44.720
call 911 immediately and be prepared to perform CPR

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.119
if they stop breathing. For inhaled poisons, move the person to fresh air

00:00:49.119 --> 00:00:51.919
right away, and for chemical burns on the skin,

00:00:51.919 --> 00:00:56.160
remember to rinse the affected area with clean water for at least 15 minutes.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.200
If you are dealing with poison oak, ivy, or sumac,

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:03.439
your goal is to remove the oils by taking off any contaminated clothing and

00:01:03.439 --> 00:01:06.160
washing the skin thoroughly with soap and water.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:09.440
You can use over-the-counter medications for the itch, but see a

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:14.000
healthcare professional if it gets worse. In many environments, you can also find a

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.000
safety data sheet, or SDS, which provides specific first aid

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.080
information for different poisons. Before moving on, I want you to consider

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.959
this question. If a child swallowed a household cleaner

00:01:24.959 --> 00:01:29.120
but is currently alert and talking, what would be your very first phone call?

